  "note": [
    "Alfie Control West's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one vehicle layout in scripts/fabric-shuttle.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. ALFIE-CONTROL-WEST.metadata.json v2: the east cabin turned half round, 2.8 x 3.0 x 4.8, the eye at the middle, the same panel mirrored -- slot, lever and display still left to right from an operator facing the window.",
    "West, the 2.45 x 0.9 forward window: at Kalamontee the station's dead end, a concrete buffer 1.8 m off, which is why this cabin cannot start the car there (shuttleActivate: only the cabin facing the tunnel is accepted); at Lawanda the bore running 51 m away west, rails on the bed 1 m below this deck.",
    "East, the 1.5 x 2.4 doorway and the car end-on: benches, the clear freight deck, the north doorway off to the left at about 6 m with the platform beyond it, and at the far end the east cabin's door with a slot of its window. From this eye the platform's cone falls on its blank east wall at both stations -- the escalator mouth at Lawanda is 1.2 m short of it -- so nothing of either station's east end is in sight."
